Week 6 — Testing Different Input Images and Videos
🎯 Objective

To test how different source images and driving videos affect the quality of the generated animation.

🛠️ Work Completed
Tested different source images and driving-video inputs.
Observed how image cropping and subject positioning affected animation.
Reviewed the generated frames for movement consistency.
Compared outputs produced using different input combinations.
⚠️ Problem Faced

Some input combinations could produce unnatural facial movement or distorted output, especially when the source image and driving video had different poses or framing.

✅ Resolution
Selected clearer source images with the subject positioned centrally.
Checked image cropping and video quality before processing.
Used shorter driving clips during initial testing to simplify troubleshooting.
🖼️ Project Picture

Comparison of source images, driving-video frames and generated animation.

💡 Learning

I learned that input quality significantly affects the final animation. Suitable images and driving videos help improve motion transfer.
